  "summary": "The German school and design language that fused art, craft and industry around geometric form, primary colors and functional honesty.",
  "description": "Founded by Walter Gropius, the Bauhaus proposed that form follows function and that everyday objects should be designed for industrial production. Its visual language — circles, triangles and squares in primary red, yellow and blue; sans-serif type; tubular steel; flat roofs and glass curtain walls — became the backbone of modernist design worldwide. Closed by the Nazis in 1933, its faculty (Gropius, Mies, Moholy-Nagy, Albers) emigrated and spread the doctrine globally. Bauhaus aesthetics remain shorthand for rational, unadorned design.",
